@startuml architecture
' The backend's layers (Phase 5); documentation/backend.puml has the classes.
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "Backend App" {
    [Middleware\nTrustedHost, CORS, BodyLimit] as Middleware
    [FastAPI Application\napi.py] as App
    [Service Layer\nbusiness_logic] as Service
    [Repository Layer\ndata_access/repository.py] as Repository
    [Database Layer\ndata_access/database.py] as Database
    [Schema Preparation\ndata_access/schema.py] as Schema
    [Models\nmodels/todo.py] as Models
    [Schemas\nschemas/] as Schemas
    [Settings\nsettings.py] as Settings
    [Logger\nlogger.py] as Logger
}

[Alembic migrations\nbackend/migrations] as Migrations
database "SQLite" as SQLite

Middleware --> App : passes requests
App --> Service : calls
App --> Schemas : validates with
App --> Settings : reads
App --> Schema : checks the revision at startup
Service --> Repository : uses
Service --> Logger : logs
Repository --> Models : maps
Repository --> Database : sessions
Database --> SQLite
Schema --> Migrations : runs
Migrations --> SQLite

note right of App
  Main entry point
  Handles API routes
end note

note right of Service
  Business logic layer
  Builds and validates todos
end note

note right of Repository
  Data access layer
  Soft delete: rows stay, flagged deleted
end note

note right of Schema
  Before serving: create the database,
  or back it up and migrate it
end note

note right of Models
  Data model
  Timestamps in UTC
end note

note right of Schemas
  Pydantic schemas
  Data validation and serialization
end note

note right of Logger
  Custom logging system
  Neutralised messages
end note
@enduml
